menu "Slideshow test app"

    config HAC_SLIDESHOW_INTERVAL_S
        int "Seconds from the end of one picture's refresh to the next"
        range 1 86400
        default 60
        help
            Every picture is a whole-panel REFRESH_FULL, about 3.3 s on this
            panel. A value below the panel's minimum full-refresh interval
            (BOARD_EPD_MIN_FULL_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS in
            platform/esp32_t5s3/board_config.h, 60 s) is raised to it at
            runtime, and the boot log says so: the slideshow drives the
            glass no harder than the product may.

    config HAC_SLIDESHOW_CAPTION
        bool "Caption each picture with its number and file name"
        default y
        help
            A small boxed "n/N name" in the bottom-left corner, so a photo
            of the panel says which picture -- and which dithering -- it
            shows. Turn it off for pictures meant to be looked at.

endmenu
